            </profile>
            <profile id="900f-6582-cb9a-4f47" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Broadsword. May have shield +2 pts, light armour +4 pts, javelins +2 pts. On foot may replace sword with double handed sword or mace +4 pts. May ride a horse (free, increase Movement to 8"). If mounted on a horse may have throwing spear +4 pts or thrusting spear +2 pts. Army General. Warband Psychology. Mountain Indian list only. 0-1 General. (Alexander the Great p.113)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="d9f2-7ebd-6f64-48fd" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
