            <profile id="f368-72fa-4203-55b9" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Special Troops (Republican Indian list only). Wagons are fielded in groups of five models minimum, each wagon is treated as a single model (based 60mm by 40mm). They may be deployed up to 12" from the player's baseline, end-to-end in a single straight line parallel to the baseline. The wagons may not be moved and are immune to psychology and cannot be broken in hand-to-hand combat. The line counts as a wall 40mm wide; each wagon model may be occupied by up to four infantry skirmishers, or characters. Units behind wagons count as in soft cover but may not use massed archery; wagons count as large targets; defenders in wagons gain a 5+ save like chariots. Attackers need 6s to hit units behind unoccupied wagons or skirmishers inside them, until the attacker wins a round of combat. Empty and undefended wagons are destroyed at the end of the Combat phase if an enemy unit of five models or more remains in contact. (Alexander the Great p.114)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="6320-b3f0-a1f1-ba4c" name="Wagon Laager (Republican)" hidden="false" targetId="b95a-4789-9033-2aa6" type="rule"/>
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="35"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
