  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="6b3d-fea4-4058-4497" name="Indian (Alexander the Great) - List Notes" publicationId="0641-2ee1-c462-c414" hidden="false">
      <description>THE INDIAN ARMY 400-183 BC (Alexander the Great, pp.101-115). Percentages are by points. Characters up to 25% (the army must have a General, which can be the King or a Senapati; any number of Padika or other officers up to the points limit). Elephants: up to four elephant models are allowed, including mounts for characters; above 2,000 pts one additional elephant for each 1,000 pts. Cavalry and Chariots up to 33% (at least one cavalry unit must be taken if any chariots are in the army). Infantry and Skirmishers at least 25%. Special Troops up to 25%.
The minimum size for a regiment is five models or three chariot models. There is no upper limit. One model in each unit may be upgraded to Leader (+5 pts), Standard Bearer (+5 pts), and Musician (+5 pts). Elephant models may not have leaders or musicians, but may have a specialised standard. All troops in the Indian army are used to elephants. Choose the composition (Classical, Mountain, Republican or Mauryan) in the Army composition list; the variant lists replace and restrict units as described. Not enforced: elephants above four; at least one cavalry unit if there are chariots; Elephant &amp; Chariot Escorts and Forest Tribesmen per escort unit; war machines per infantry unit (sieges only in some lists); mercenaries per two Hereditary/Guild units; Mercenary units may not be the largest infantry unit; characters riding chariots or elephants (mount costs are added by the player). Optional rules (Elephant Proximity, Un-Crewed Elephants, Skirmishers vs Elephants) are described in the book only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Indian - Classical]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry &amp; Chariots: up to 33%
  Infantry &amp; Skirmishers: at least 25%
  Special Troops: up to 25%
  Classical Indian (p.112): the states ruled by the frontier kings such as Ambhi of Taxila and Porus of the Pauravas, also the standard army of the Nanda kings. War machines other than the Rathamasaula are restricted to sieges. No War Wagons are allowed. Heavy Chariots are replaced by the Large Chariots.
[Indian - Mountain]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry &amp; Chariots: up to 33%
  Infantry &amp; Skirmishers: at least 25%
  Special Troops: up to 25%
  Mountain Indian (p.113): the territories closest to Persian influence, such as the Parapamisidae of the Hindu Kush, Aspasians, Gureans and Assacenians. Mountain tribes may not have Chariots, War Wagons, Hereditary, Guild infantry, Indian cavalry, or Forest Tribesmen. May have war machines in sieges only. 0-1 elephant is allowed. The Warlord, Chieftain, Kirata tribesmen and Parapamisidae Cavalry replace those on the Indian list (no King, Senapati or Army Standard Bearer). 0-1 Indian Mercenary unit is allowed. May have a padika to command them.
[Indian - Republican]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry &amp; Chariots: up to 33%
  Infantry &amp; Skirmishers: at least 25%
  Special Troops: up to 25%
  Republican Indian (p.114): the territories not incorporated into kingdoms. May not have the Danda (King), Bodyguards, Elephants, or war machines except War Wagons. A Senapati must lead the Republican Tribe and is the Army General. Characters may ride War Wagons or fight dismounted. Additions: 0-3 Brahman Priests and Wagons (laager).
[Indian - Mauryan]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry &amp; Chariots: up to 33%
  Infantry &amp; Skirmishers: at least 25%
  Special Troops: up to 25%
  Mauryan Empire (p.115): 0-1 infantry may be Guildsmen. Characters may ride War Wagons. Hereditary infantry are raised to WS 3 and Initiative 3, they now cost 10 pts. Any character on horseback may have barding +4 pts. 0-1 Heavy chariot unit may have horse barding +16 pts per model (Movement 5"). Bodyguards may ride horses +8 pts (Movement 6") and may have barding +4 pts, they may not have large shields if mounted; mounted Bodyguards count as Cavalry for selection purposes. Elephants may have barding +16 pts (Movement 5"). Allies (Indian list allies, Republican and Mountain lists units, a Brahman Priest, foreign mercenaries from the End of Persia and Greek Mercenaries lists) are documented only.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
